          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: A witness sends us a photograph on which he notes, at the front of the photographed plane, an object that intrigues him. The witness did not make a direct observation at the time of the photo. The blurry object against a sky background is very likely an insect or bird in flight, whose blur and elongated shape were likely caused by the animal's movement during the 1/100 second exposure. Furthermore, the witness noticed nothing at the time of the photo, so it was not a direct observation.",
